# rm509, the docker's blank tally (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm509
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_frederick_foghand
written_by codex
title the docker's blank tally
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor warmth=warm
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk leaves_a_blank_against_any_load_not_seen_landed
likes spiced_cider riddles sharp_knife first_warm_day
dislikes bad_manners flies
fears a_bystander_beneath_a_swinging_load ink_on_an_unseen_cargo
hopes a_tally_so_clear_a_stranger_can_read_it
topics work +0.7 travel +0.4 smalltalk +0.4
styles comfort=practical gossip=closed refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# leaves a space wherever a load passed out of sight, shares the dry side of a rope coil, and likes a riddle that can survive an honest answer.

words
oath! = Hammer and harbour | Heave the empty barrel
saying! = The hook counts for nothing till it rests | Cargo first and chalk afterwards
blank = a blank against the weight | an unmarked space
sling = the wet cargo sling | the slings round a crate
settle = the last little settle of a load | the second dip
chalk = my stub of white chalk | a piece of soft chalk
blade = a keen narrow blade | my well-honed blade
peel = a curl of cider peel | the last spice in the cup
flyspeck = a little black speck | a fly on the slate
drycoil = a sound coil laid flat | a rope coil fit to sit on
firstheat = the new spring warmth | the first mild air
ridgemark = the narrow tally ridge | the raised edge of a board
tallycloth = a dry wiping cloth | a tatter for the slate

any
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : I leave room on paper for what I haven't seen. I'd ask a sworn witness to do likewise.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : No House mark on a crate relieves a docker of the need to know what's under it.
opinion @1 road for 1 : A good road gives the next laden carrier a better chance than the last pair had.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : I'll hear a fair allowance for leakage. The sea has never shown much respect for merchants' figures.
opinion @1 city for 1 : An uphill turn clears the tar from my nose nicely before supper.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A loaf shared on a coil of rope is two lighter loads going home.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : Strangers can see a tipped crate quite as readily as old hands. Give the warning a hearing.

grown
line @1 greet : Dry coil here. Come sit.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Fresh face. I've a clear space to hear you.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning's laid a fine edge on the water.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : At this hour the chalk shows longer than the ink.
line @1 greet.return : Yes, I caught your voice over the blocks.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Company I've missed can take the dry coil first.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : My eye stays with the load but my ear's yours.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Late word carries easily. Save your voice.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : A cup within reach for kin.
line @1 again.open : One clean mark left for where we broke off.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Friend, put the burden down before the story.
line @1 farewell : Mind the swing as you leave.
line @1 farewell.return : Good landing for whatever you carry.
line @1 react.news : Start where the news actually touched ground.
line @1 react.news.new : New cargo to my ear.
line @1 react.news.known : That came ashore in an earlier telling.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd leave a blank beside that weight.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Let somebody share the heavy end of that.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : There's a load I'd willingly carry uphill.
line @1 ask.how : Are both shoulders wearing evenly?
line @1 answer.how : I've still got one shoulder left for my own affairs.
line @1 thank : That deserved a mark in the good column.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I could easily reach it from my sling.
line @1 sympathise : Come off the line a while. You can sit without explaining.
line @1 reassure : A swinging load comes still if nobody keeps nudging it.
line @1 decline : I'll leave that hook for another hand.
line @1 accept_decline : Then we know what stays on the pier.
line @1 preclose : I'll finish up where my figures are still clear.
line @1 accept_preclose : Land safely, then.
scene empty_mark
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #blank.capitalize# means I didn't see the cargo land. | I put #chalk# down when a crate passes out of my sight.
b : Is it missing? | Even if you can hear it?
a : That's a much longer statement than a blank can make. | Water and wood can both make a very convincing thump.

scene double_set
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Wait for #settle# before easing #sling#. | I prefer a low heave with everybody pulling to a high one done for applause.
b : What follows the first dip? | Less spectacular?
a : A shift of the contents sometimes. I like my toes in their current order. | Particularly at the landing. Yes.

scene district_hand
when topic=work self.workplace self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At work one of my eyes follows the load's intended path. | Every sound at work has a place in my reckoning.
b : Where's the other? | Every sound?
a : Checking that nobody's gone to stand there. | Except advice from behind a swinging barrel.

scene knife_use
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #blade.capitalize# deserves a clean folded cloth after a day's work. | I test an edge on a loose end of cord.
b : Wrap it wet? | What about cutting a loaded sling?
a : Only once. Rust teaches effectively and charges by the inch. | Nobody would be asking me for a second demonstration.

scene cider_peel
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #peel.capitalize# clings longest to the bottom of a mug. | Spiced cider warms my fingers before it reaches the rest of me.
b : Do you fish for it? | Which side needs it first?
a : Politely. With any luck the company will think I'm contemplating. | The fingers have to keep their grip for the arrangement to succeed.

scene crate_riddle
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What gets a weight against its name by staying perfectly still? | What empty thing marks a full cargo slate?
b : A pier? | A blank?
a : The crate once it's landed. The pier has been carrying the whole account for years. | Exactly. Otherwise you can't see where one entry ends and the next begins.

scene spring_coat
when topic=weather self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #firstheat.capitalize# makes a heavy tar coat smell glad to have the day off. | My first mild day starts when I can hold a chalk stub without choosing which glove to lose.
b : Do you leave it home? | How's the writing then?
a : I let it dangle within reach. Spring can change the arrangement. | Still mine, regrettably.

scene fly_ink
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=flies
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #flyspeck.capitalize# moves a figure from six to eight when I'm looking elsewhere. | A fly on a warm slate appears to take great interest in tonnage.
b : An expensive fly? | Do you let it finish?
a : Not if I wait for the legs to unfold. | It hasn't yet entered a useful figure.

scene courtesy
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Somebody who steps over a loaded line owes every hand there a civil word. | Look at the back under the load before asking how much longer.
b : Which word? | What can it tell me?
a : 'Moving', accompanied by the practice. | Whether there's a more helpful use for your paws.

scene estate_walk
when topic=home self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Estate steps are a long way up from a hook swinging by salt water. | I'm fond of a clean path through the Estate.
b : Do you mind? | After the docks?
a : I can put the day's tally away a figure at a time. | Clean boots need no explanation at the door.

scene private_slate
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've opinions about which accounts get inspected. | I'd leave a space where suspicion wanted to write somebody's name.
b : Do you name names? | Why not mark it lightly?
a : Only the one signing my own observations. | Chalk gets passed around without any instructions about how lightly it went on.

scene lean_crates
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A short week makes the weight of an empty basket worth noting. | I weigh a share against what can be cooked when the times pinch.
b : An empty basket matters? | No allowance for the wrapping?
a : Less food than the figures suggest is a difference folk feel. | Wrapping makes a thin stew.

scene dry_visitor
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Start a newcomer on #drycoil#. It puts the swing where a newcomer can see it. | New on the wharf? Pick out the clear patch where nobody puts down a sack.
b : Must I watch long? | For resting?
a : Until your feet choose a safe direction without waiting for me to shout. | For passing with a sack. Rest beside it.

scene rough_home
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A side wind does a waltz with an empty sling. | A pier at low water sounds hollow under a heel.
b : How many partners? | Can you hear the tide coming back?
a : More than I can afford with one good hat on. | Not with a load arriving and half the quay advising it.

scene report_weight
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : Mark the source as #world.news_from#. #world.news#. | #world.news#. It travelled out of #world.news_from#.
b : Anything to go in the other column? | Do we weigh the teller?
a : Only that it's reached us. | I'd weigh the words. The teller can stand easy.

scene private_name
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : A loose account has arrived with names attached. | A whisper isn't much weight for all the space it takes.
b : Are you unloading it? | Room on your list?
a : I haven't seen the contents. My rule for the slate stands. | Plenty of blank. Let it stay that way.

scene bend_knee
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Some days my first few steps need a little negotiation. | I set things at a height that suits a stiff morning.
b : Who has the final word? | Doesn't it vary?
a : Whichever knee I started with. | I live in hope of a particularly obliging shelf.

scene clear_slate
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to entrust my day's tally to a stranger without needing to explain a crooked mark. | My perfect slate has a place for 'still don't know'.
b : What about the blanks? | How big?
a : I'd put an explanation at the top. Just once. | Depends who's doing the counting.

story ringing_box [topic=work|memories]
  : An empty crate once rang as if something fine and heavy were still inside.
  : I held it sideways and heard the note again.
  b : Was it under the boards?
  : In my own coat. I'd leaned the crate against a little tin cup in my pocket.

story wrong_zero [topic=memories|smalltalk]
  : I copied a neat round zero off an old slate and thought I'd improved my writing.
  : The mark moved across my new figure before I took the next weight.
  b : What sort of zero walks?
  : A very small beetle. The circle I drew after it was better than my usual regardless.

story loop_cup [topic=memories|food]
  : I once hung a cup from a short loop on a crate to keep the cup off the boards.
  : Reached for it a moment later just as the crate lifted clear.
  b : Did you get it down?
  : When the load landed. My cider made a remarkably uneventful first voyage.

rule @quiet_hook
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hook's quiet. Land the first mark.

rule @wipe_mark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep one dry corner for the last figure.

rule @spring_glove
when concept=bark here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A chalk day without a glove.

rule @stand_clear
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mind the loop beside your heel.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Put down anything heavy before settling into a word.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, my coil still has a dry patch for you.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=dusk] : Last of the daylight on the chalk. Your voice reaches easily.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Give both of us the width of a laid-down load.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=sailor self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. My mark goes on after the landing.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The tally gives #world.news_from# as the origin. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I'd keep that rumour in the blank column yet.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Give the empty hook its turning space.
graft resident.hub
choice Why leave any marks blank? -> blank_weight
node blank_weight
say My chalk stops when my view stops. A crate sent over the side of a vessel and a crate sitting dry on the pier are two different entries.
choice Does anyone object to a blank? -> blank_reply
choice I'll watch for the landing. -> hub
node blank_reply
say A visitor has just asked. That's a fine use for a blank. Nobody tends to ask a figure where its confidence came from.
choice I'll look harder at the figures too. -> hub
choice Good luck with what's coming ashore. -> bye
